# Application Architecture Brief

Cloudflare Agent Dungeon is a Turborepo app with a small shared domain core and a Cloudflare Worker runtime.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Domain["packages/domain
Schemas + pure rules
AdventureModule / TableRun / Campaign"]
  Worker["apps/worker
Cloudflare Agent body
routes + monitor UI
town forge + run loop"]
  Minds["Think minds
RefereeAgent + PlayerAgents
typed proposals, not truth"]
  Store["Storage / artifacts
R2 skill/artifact files
event logs + receipts"]

  Domain -->|types + rules| Worker
  Worker -->|prompts + tools| Minds
  Minds -->|typed proposals| Worker
  Worker -->|persist| Store
  Worker -->|validated state| Domain
```


## In one breath

- `packages/domain` is the durable game model: Zod schemas, table-run state, adventure modules, campaign events, dice, clocks, treasure/XP hooks, and projection helpers.
- `apps/worker` is the Cloudflare runtime: HTTP routes, Agent/Think integration, AI calls, the town/module forge, live monitor pages, and persistence wiring.
- The Referee owns canonical truth. Player minds see projections and return typed proposals; they do not mutate hidden state directly.
- Runtime artifacts live outside the public monitor boundary. Public UI gets sanitized projections, not private Referee notes or raw rules corpus.

## Source receipts

- `package.json` — Turborepo scripts and workspace shape.
- `packages/domain/src/index.ts` — core campaign types, events, projections, and rule helpers.
- `packages/domain/src/adventure-module.ts` — generic `AdventureModule` and visibility projection boundary.
- `packages/domain/src/table-run.ts` — table-run lifecycle, events, phases, combat/encounter helpers, summaries.
- `apps/worker/src/index.ts` — Cloudflare Agent/Think imports, Worker routes, AI/object generation, R2 skill/artifact integration.
